Track 2: Veredicto de cobre
- Story & Context: Sofia stood atop the storm-drenched cliff, clutching her copper-laced cloak as she demanded an answer from the sky for the silence left behind by her missing brother. When the storm finally struck the rod beside her, her voice morphed into a distorted, demonic scream, shouting "Dime por qué el cielo guarda secretos de hierro." The piano roared beneath her, a cacophony of metal on wood that sounded like a building collapsing. 
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A cinematic portrait of a woman in a conductive copper-woven garment standing under a black sky, shards of lightning reflecting in her eyes, raw industrial energy.

Track 3: Undelivered Postmarked Rage
- Story & Context: Years after the radio station dissolved into myth, a bag of letters arrived at the town square, all of them postmarked from the heart of the great 1996 storm, each page stained with iron filings. They contained no words, only musical notation that, when played, caused the neighborhood pianos to ignite in a symphony of percussive fury. "Somos la señal que nunca llegaste a sintonizar," the final ghost-track chanted, marking the end of the legend that demanded we never stop looking for the lightning. 
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A rain-soaked pile of ancient letters scattered on dark cobblestones, glowing faint blue from hidden electricity, melancholic yet explosive atmosphere.

